          %p
            hence that both rows are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact
          %p We record the following immediate consequence of this definition (which, in the literature, is often taken to be the definition).
          #LeftRightExactFunctorsCharacterizedByExactSequences.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a left exact functor, then for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to A \to B \to C,
            %p also
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
