          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          %p The following proposition says that, in degree 0, these derived functors coincide with the original functors.
          #BasicPropertiesOfDerivedFunctors.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact functor
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftRightExactFunctor"}
              in the presence of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enough+injectives"} enough injectives
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒜
